{"title":"Evans point","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The Evans point is the intersection point of the Gergonne line and the Euler line. It has triangle center function and is Kimberling center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887dc375340294021fa98d350efdc8697dcce362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{1375}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Evans_point.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/b1/Evans_point.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"459\" height=\"279\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Weisstein, Eric W. \"Evans Point.\" From MathWorld--A Wolfram Web Resource. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://mathworld.wolfram.com/EvansPoint.html\">http://mathworld.wolfram.com/EvansPoint.html</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Evans_point&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082751\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 178/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.229      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.229      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15655:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082751 and revision id 86840. Rendering was triggered 